Review written to `docs/reviews/tests/test-02-integration-test-coverage.md`. Summary:

- **11 findings**: 1 critical, 4 high, 4 medium, 2 low
- **Critical**: Checkpoint/restart compares only `net_electric_power_kw` — zone temps, equipment states, RNG are unchecked
- **Key high findings**: Determinism compares only per-end-use totals (not trajectories), `aggregation_check.rs` is missing (breaks the regression suite), fleet test uses only identical dwellings, checkpoint never tested on real HPXML
- **Equipment gaps**: PV-only, EV-only, electric resistance, gas WH, HPWH, and combined PV+battery+EV fixtures exist but have no dedicated integration tests exercising full state machines
- **Seasonal gap**: Summer/winter tests use different buildings, so seasonal effects can't be distinguished from building effects
